This reads `flags` (2 bytes). Fine.

Let me reconsider. Maybe the READ 8 is in the `memcpy` in `_write_glyf_and_loca_prime`. When `memcpy` copies data, it may read 8 bytes at a time. If the source buffer is at the end of the allocated memory, reading 8 bytes could go past the end. But this is a general memcpy behavior.

